<section id="about">
  <span class="hero-ornament"></span>
  <h1 class="research-title">About the Institute</h1>
  <p class="research-subtitle">Who we are, how we work, and how to reach us.</p>
  <p class="about-lede">The Epoch Institute researches human civilisation with objectivity and curiosity: the rise and fall of states, empires and cultures, the present-day echoes of historical events, and the ways the past shapes modern society. We aim to make the story of humanity not just informative but compelling. History is not a closed book; it is the foundation of everything around us.</p>
  <div class="research-grid about-grid">

    <div class="research-card" id="methodology">
      <div class="research-card-icon">⊞</div>
      <h3 class="research-card-title">How we work</h3>
      <ul class="about-how">
        <li><b>Profiles</b> are written from the works listed in each profile&#8217;s references and checked for accuracy; every page shows when it was last reviewed.</li>
        <li><b>Power scores</b> (0&#8211;10) are the Institute&#8217;s interpretive judgements of a state&#8217;s strength over time, based on those works. Each curve is scaled to its own peak: compare the shapes, not the sizes.</li>
        <li><b>The encyclopedia and the states register</b> are compiled by the Institute. Pictures come from Wikimedia Commons under free licences, credited under each one.</li>
        <li><b>Maps</b> place each state at its capital or seat, from Wikidata (CC0), on Natural Earth outlines (public domain).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="research-card">
      <div class="research-card-icon">✉</div>
      <h3 class="research-card-title">Get in touch</h3>
      <p class="research-card-desc">Spotted an error? Want to suggest a state or a theme, write for us, or work with us? Every message reaches the research team.</p>
      <div class="about-chips"><a href="/contact?topic=correction">Correct an error</a><a href="/contact?topic=suggest">Suggest a topic</a><a href="/contact?topic=press">Partnerships</a></div>
      <a class="research-card-cta" href="/contact">Contact the Institute &rarr;</a>
    </div>

  </div>
